# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

## Overview
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the webtoon-recommend-frontend project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@latest` package using npm
- Package version: Added to dependencies in package.json
- Lock file updated: package-lock.json

### 2. Code Changes
**File Modified:** `src/App.tsx`

- Added import statement for Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Wrapped the main application content with a React Fragment (`<>...</>`)
- Placed the `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component
- This ensures analytics tracking is active throughout the entire application

### 3. Implementation Details
According to the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), for React/Vite projects:
- The `@vercel/analytics/react` package provides the React-specific Analytics component
- The component should be placed at the root level of the application
- No additional configuration is required in code
- Analytics will automatically track page views and web vitals once deployed to Vercel

### 4. Verification Steps Completed
✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ All 11 existing tests passed (`npm test`)
✅ No linting errors introduced
✅ Lock file properly updated with new dependency

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard
2. Visit the deployed site to generate initial analytics data
3. Verify tracking is working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after user traffic accumulates

## Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- It automatically respects user privacy settings and GDPR compliance
- Data collection begins only after the project is deployed to Vercel and Analytics is enabled in the dashboard
